From: PARP LZX v4.2
Subject: parp: enable reclaim-bin ordering for policy-owned memcg subtrees

The reclaim target in the trained-sequence experiment is the parent slice.
It intentionally has no application binding; its descendant GUI/fixture scopes
carry the application domains and LSTM scores.  Requiring the parent itself to
produce an application score left the non-root reclaim ordering path disabled.

Add parp_tier2_reclaim_bin_order_enabled() to distinguish policy ownership from
application scoring.  shrink_node_memcgs() now enables ordered subtree walks
when the target has an enabled Tier2 policy ancestor, then continues to score
each descendant independently.  OFF and targets outside an enabled policy
subtree retain the native iterator path.

Files:
- include/linux/parp_tier2.h
- mm/parp/core/watermark.c
- mm/vmscan.c

